            "review_title": "Review at Mi Quang My Son Restaurant",
            "review_text": "Wingc633\nHong Kong, China2070 contributions\n0\nCheap but delicious\nJun 2016 • Friends\nIt was a Vietnamese noodles chain shop. The shop was not so big, it was about 100 square meters. Most customers were locals. The air-conditioner inside the shop was not so efficient, so do not expect you would have a comfort environment when you taking a hot bowl of noodles. \nI went there with my friends on 6 June 2016. They brought me there, we ordered four bowl of pork and chicken noodles, together with 2 pieces of crispy rice cakes. The noodles were delicious especially when I dipped the rice cake into the soup which absorb the essence of the soup.\nThe price was so cheap, it was around 2 US dollars per bowl.\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten June 9, 2016",
